 ],
 "notes": "Garden street (south) facade from the view across the railed garden and the street corner view: a long pale brick front, its western two thirds cantilevered a little over the ground floor, a two-storey ribbon of glass with a pale metal spandrel, patches and bands of open-bond perforated brick, a recessed glass slot at the west party wall. North facade from the dusk view: a brick stair tower standing clear of the roof, a lower eastern part with punched windows and brick lattices at ground level, and a second cantilevered volume with two ribbon windows to the west, the entrance under the tower. Plot size estimated from storey and door heights (~36 x 22 m); depth, roof and the side streets were not photographed and are guessed; the preserved washhouse under its glass floor is inside and not shown. The brick is a pale grey-beige, not red, so it is drawn as stone (the nearest colour); the red brick material is kept for the neighbouring houses against the party walls."
